  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalGetQuest.CantSayYoure": "You can't say you're much aware of Akbal. You may have heard of a jaguar at some point, perhaps, but if so it has slipped your mind."
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalGetQuest.ClarifiesHerSmug": "[pg][say: Not quite,] Fera clarifies, [say: I gave him a quest of sorts--a set of objectives he must accomplish to gain my blessing. Not everyone gets the opportunity to free me, some actually have to work to gain my favor.] Her smug expression as she says that is entirely unwelcome, you feel. She continues, finally reaching the point of all this, [say: I want you to go out into the woods and find him. In whatever manner you so choose, get in his way. Kick him around, claim his objectives before him, or just spit in his face to provoke him; I care not how you obstruct his quest. 'Happy hunting', [name].]"
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalGetQuest.GodOfTerrestrialFire": "[pg][say: He calls himself 'God of the Terrestrial Fire', and speaks with telepathy to overcome his rather feral limitations. While he may move with the natural grace of a jaguar, and even hunt like one, he is truly just a demon bound to that form by a curse.]"
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalGetQuest.GoddessShiftsPosition": "[pg][say: He tracked me down and approached me.] The goddess shifts position as she pushes her hair back over her shoulder, explaining the situation as she does. [say: Akbal knows full well about the Goddess of Predation, and claims himself apex predator of this forest in hopes of gaining my boon. Those who served my sister created the seal on him, surely I would be able to break that seal.] Fera gives a haughty smirk, saying [say: Of course, I could do that with no particular effort.]"
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalGetQuest.GoddessStrutsOn": "[pg]The goddess struts on through her garden, not waiting for any answers. Inexplicably, your mind is completely clear. The dizzying fumes of this place aren't messing with you any longer, allowing you to leave without a problem. As you head home, you think over the proposition..."
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalGetQuest.IndeedYouDoKnow": "Indeed you do know about the demon-beast. He calls himself God of the Terrestrial Fire, though it's clear enough to you that he is just a demon rather than a god."
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalGetQuest.SoThenThere": "[pg]So then there is a fully strengthened and unleashed Akbal roaming the world once more?"
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalGetQuest.ThatSaidDidntStop": " That said, it didn't stop you from worshiping him..."
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalGetQuest.WhyBringUpAkbal": "[pg]Why bring up Akbal now, though? He certainly couldn't be a problem for an actual god, why would Fera care to mention him?"
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalQuestIntro.EffortsToStayFocused": "[pg]Your efforts to keep yourself focused and steady amidst the noxious air adds a degree of tension to the conversation. This goddess is not quite as benevolent as her sister {0}; there is a feeling of danger even when she thanks you. Fera takes a moment to bask in the fumes of her twisted garden before continuing to speak to you."
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalQuestIntro.FamiliarWithA": "[pg][say: Tell me, dear champion, are you familiar with a jaguar by the name of 'Akbal'?]"
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalQuestIntro.ShadowPassesTheEdge": "A shadow passes the edge of your vision. You turn to look only to catch a glimpse from the opposite direction. A gentle giggle echoes around you."
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalQuestIntro.TurnAroundHeadOut": "You turn around and head out. You trudge through the vegetation for several minutes, growing more dizzy and confused as you don't seem to reach the edge of the glade. Something isn't right. "
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalQuestIntro.TurnForwardYetAgain": "[pg]As you turn forward yet again, the fair-skinned goddess titters, her fiery-orange tresses hanging down around you in a corrupted halo, drawing your gaze to her pale, creamy skin, prominent ruby lips, and smoldering red eyes. Dazed by her drug-exuding flowers though you are, you haven't given up anything like you did when you freed her. You raise your [weapon], staring down Fera, Goddess of Predation. She smirks."
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalQuestIntro.WasJustHopingYoud": "[pg][say: Oh, [name], I was just hoping you'd visit my glade{0}. Don't you love it?] she says, as you back away from her invasive closeness. You are not prey to be trapped by pretty flowers. [say: Of course you aren't. You are strong, as my champion should be. You are a <b>predator</b>.] She rolls the <i>predator</i> term into almost a growl as it passes through her vocal chords."
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraAkbalQuestIntro.WhileWalkingThrough": "While you're walking through the deepest, darkest parts of these overgrown woodlands, you come across a wild glade, filled with hundreds and hundreds of the most beautiful blossoming flowers. They cover the hundred or so feet across the clearing densely, some small, like dandelions and orchids, others enormous, on stalks as thick as small tree-trunks, blooming so vibrantly that you find yourself rubbing your eyes after gazing at them, dazzled by their many hued palettes. Sweet aromas of a thousand types of flowers blend together into a symphony of nasal delight, and you breathe deep as a nagging sense of familiarity fills your thoughts. "
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraSceneTwoIntroduction.CreepingShiverCrawls": "[pg]A creeping shiver crawls down your back until you straighten and take in your surroundings once more. This place is too pretty for you to stay down in the dumps for too long, and besides, a particularly intriguing fragrance is tickling your nose. It seems to come from the center of the glade, where the biggest, most vibrant blooms have sprouted. Do you want to explore the center, around some of the huge flowers, or head back to the safety of your camp?"
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraSceneTwoIntroduction.FlopBackIntoSoft": "[pg]You flop back into the soft grasses that ring this overwhelmingly sweet glade. The nectar-sweet ambrosia that's carried through the air on clouds of pollen ought to be attracting some insects, shouldn't it? You glance around, looking for the bees and butterflies you would normally expect to thrive in such a place, but there are none. No bugs, no gnats, no aphids... just flowers... flowers everywhere. You get up and wander around a little bit, looking this way and that, hunting for any proof of life while simultaneously taking in the cacophony of dazzling colors."
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraSceneTwoIntroduction.HereSpotProof": "[pg]Here and there, you spot proof of Mareth's corruption in this seemingly pristine place: a flower whose petals look like plump, red lips, just waiting to be kissed, vines with distinctly phallic shapes protruding from the central stalk of the flower, and flowers whose entrances shine with slick fluids and part at your approach, appearing very much like a pair of clingy, virginal folds. And still, there are no bees. You run to the edge of the blooming meadow, and there, at last, you find what you were looking for."
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraSceneTwoIntroduction.SingleNormalLookingBee": "[pg]A single, normal-looking bee, is lazily buzzing down onto a flower a few inches away, heedless of your presence. It homes right in on the sweet-smelling divot in the center of the petals, touching down without slowing or stopping to investigate the new arrival. Instead, it crawls deeper into the floral creases, hunting pollen and nectar. The petals snap up and around, slamming together with the speed of a clockwork trap, their edges seamlessly joined together into a single, entrapping sphere, perfectly encapsulating the poor insect. You hear a muffled buzz as the bug vainly attempts to escape, and then nothing. Whatever happened inside, the bee isn't struggling anymore."
  "Scenes.Fera.FeraSceneTwoIntroduction.WhileWalkingThrough": "While you're walking through the deepest, darkest parts of these overgrown woodlands, you come across a wild glade, filled with hundreds and hundreds of the most beautiful blossoming flowers. They cover the hundred or so feet across the clearing densely, some small, like dandelions and orchids, others enormous, on stalks as thick as small tree-trunks, blooming so vibrantly that you find yourself rubbing your eyes after gazing at them, dazzled by their many hued palettes. Sweet aromas of a thousand types of flowers blend together into a symphony of nasal delight, and you breathe deep, laughing loudly and openly at this wondrous find."
  "Scenes.Fera.FistPumpkin.RelaxedByVapors": "Relaxed by the vapors wafting around you, you elect to accept the request of this disembodied voice. Baring the flesh of your hand to the open air, you slowly press your fist into the cavernous hole. The fleshy innards of the opening press and squeeze your arms as you sink further in, stopping at the elbow. There you linger, pondering what purpose this would serve, until the tightness suddenly increases. This isn't alarming at first, but that changes immediately when you feel thorns running through your flesh. You groan and attempt to pull free, panic setting in as blood rushes from the wounds in your arm. Just as you fear passing out, the gourd releases you, sending you tumbling back. The wounds across your [skin] have already closed, though moving your digits leaves you very sore. You'd marvel at your hand more, but a quake takes your attention."
